.TH GETRLIMIT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
getrlimit \- read a process resource limit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/resource.h>
.B int getrlimit(int resource, struct rlimit* limits);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the soft and hard limits for a Linux RLIMIT_* selector.  Limits use
rlim_t; RLIM_INFINITY indicates no limit.  Crunch uses the POSIX int selector;
GNU libc with GNU extensions declares an enum selector instead.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR getrusage (3crunch),
.BR getrlimit (2)
